# Task12 authoritative legacy configuration correction

Task12 Ruling: [62] Correct R61's inaccurate inherited empty-search-path assertion without rewriting R61 or its reason/cost history. Root read the archived legacy source and captured installed target: update_group_enquiry_with_audit(p_enquiry_id uuid,p_actor_user_id uuid,p_expected_updated_at timestamptz,p_patch jsonb), postgres SECURITY DEFINER, service-only EXECUTE, config search_path=public, pg_temp. For this minimal existing group repair, preserve that exact actual configuration and argument order; add only R61's qualified auth.users and public.admin_user SHARE fences. All group/audit relation references must remain schema-qualified. No new helper or definer conversion is introduced; the general empty-path guidance remains for new privileged helpers. Final actual temp-shadow and full unchanged scanner/call-closure checks are mandatory; if an unqualified resolution defect is reproduced, report it for its own narrow decision instead of silently changing config/helper contracts. R61's behavioral RED and all other scope/grant/role/audit/version/proof boundaries remain. Reason: the implementer identified, and root verified, that the authoritative old function uses public,pg_temp; pretending it was empty would hide configuration drift in a supposedly minimal actor repair. Cost if wrong: retaining a public/temp search path could leave a callable-resolution risk, so qualified references, full callable metadata and real shadow tests must demonstrate the actual command boundary; silently normalizing it would misstate compatibility. This correction authorizes no production/release or heldTask1/8 change.
